(Page 1: Finding relevant text) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PDF RAG Workspace lets you read a PDF beside a chat and ask questions grounded in the) Tj T*
(document. The server extracts selectable text from each physical PDF page and chunks) Tj T*
(each page separately. MiniLM converts chunks into 384-dimensional embeddings.) Tj T*
(PostgreSQL with pgvector compares a question embedding with stored chunk embeddings) Tj T*
(using cosine similarity. Retrieval is restricted to the selected document owned by) Tj T*
(the authenticated account. The server sends the retrieved text to Groq as context and) Tj T*
(asks it to answer only from that context. Answers stream back to the browser using) Tj T*
(server-sent events over a fetch request. If the context does not provide an answer,) Tj T*
(the model is instructed to say it could not find the answer. Model answers can still) Tj T*
(be wrong; check the supporting passage.) Tj T*
